	echo ""
	echo "	Note:"
	echo "	    Pass the options as one string. Single and double quotes inside that string group arguments."
	echo "	    Outside single quotes, a backslash escapes the next character. There is no shell expansion."
	echo "	    For a value containing spaces, for example, use --curl-options '--user \"myuser1:my secret\"'."
	echo "	    Long options accept --option=value or --option value; short options need a separate value."
	echo "	    Abbreviations and combined short options are not supported. Repeating this option replaces the list."
	echo "	    Conditional and Range headers, header files and multiline header values are not supported."
	echo "	    The default .curlrc is ignored so it cannot add transfers or change the output destination."
	echo ""
	echo "--debug"
	echo "	This option enables the debug mode. Should be the first option for best results."
	echo "	Bash tracing can expose URLs and credentials in the output."
	echo ""
	echo "--disable-etag"
	echo "	This option disables the usage of the ‘ETag’ cache validation method. In general, ETag should be"
	echo "	preferred for cache validation, but some servers have changing ETags, although the file hasn't changed."
	echo "	In that case, the ‘Last-modified’ header is your only option (when supported by the server)."
	echo ""
	echo "--disable-remote-time"
	echo "	By default, when a file is downloaded, its timestamp is set to match the one from the remote file."
	echo "	However, it is sometimes useful to base the local file's timestamp on when it was actually downloaded;"
	echo "	for that purpose, the ‘--disable-remote-time’ option has been provided."
	echo "	When the downloaded content is unchanged, the existing file and its timestamp are retained."
	echo ""
	echo "--enable-caching"
	echo "	This option enables the intelligent update mechanism. When this option is set,"
	echo "	the application uses ETag or Last-Modified validation when the HTTP(S) server supports it."
